<title>USA: NYCE cotton called to open little changed.</title>
<headline>NYCE cotton called to open little changed.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYCE cotton futures were called to open mostly unchanged Monday based on market orders at 1020 EST, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;We need some news,&quot; a trader said, adding that Tuesday's committment of traders report should provide some fuel for the market.</p>
<p>Friday, the benchmark March contract ended 0.05 lower at 74.60 cents, after trading from 75.25 to 74.35 cents. The back months settled 0.25 lower to 0.23 firmer.</p>
<p>Volume was estimated at 18,000 lots.</p>
<p>((--Suzanne Rostler, New York Commodities, 212 859 1640))</p>
